a b and c all happen at the same time  right well they appear to occur in a  different order depending on the  observer's reference frame this is a key  Concept in Albert Einstein's special  theory of relativity in which it's  impossible to say if two events occurred  at the same time if those events are  separated in space in real life a car  crash in New York and another in Prague  appear to occur at the same time to an  observer on Earth however they will  appear to have occurred at different  times to someone flying between New York  and Prague
 

